      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "See equivalent in the Servlet stack"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "xref",
                    "target": "web/webmvc/mvc-controller/ann.html#mvc-ann-requestmapping-proxying"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "span",
                "roles": [
                  "small"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In some cases, you may need to decorate a controller with an AOP proxy at runtime. One example is if you choose to have "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Transactional"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " annotations directly on the controller. When this is the case, for controllers specifically, we recommend using class-based proxying. This is automatically the case with such annotations directly on the controller."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If the controller implements an interface, and needs AOP proxying, you may need to explicitly configure class-based proxying. For example, with "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@EnableTransactionManagement"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " you can change to "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@EnableTransactionManagement(proxyTargetClass = true)"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", and with "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "<tx:annotation-driven/>"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " you can change to "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "<tx:annotation-driven proxy-target-class=\"true\"/>"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Keep in mind that as of 6.0, with interface proxying, Spring WebFlux no longer detects controllers based solely on a type-level "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@RequestMapping"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " annotation on the interface. Please, enable class based proxying, or otherwise the interface must also have an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Controller"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " annotation."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "note"
          }
        ],
